FAQ = [
 ("Can I mount a cargo box on the Outback's factory swing-out crossbars?",
  "Usually, yes. Most 2020–2025 Outbacks have raised rails with crossbars that stow inside the rails and swing out when you need them. A box clamps to them like any other bar, as long as the distance between the deployed bars falls inside the box's spread range, such as 24–34.5 in for the Yakima SkyBox 16. Deploy the bars, measure center to center, and compare before you buy."),
 ("How much weight can a 2020–2025 Outback roof carry with a box?",
  "Check the owner's manual for your model year, because published figures differ. Our fitment data lists 176 lb for the standard Outback, and one reference quotes 150 lb for 2020–2022 models. Plan around the lower number until you've read your manual. Then subtract the bars and the box: a 47 lb SkyBox 16 on 150 lb leaves about 100 lb for gear."),
 ("Is the Outback Wilderness roof different for a cargo box?",
  "Yes. The Wilderness uses its own heavier-duty roof rails, rated for up to 700 lb static, which is the parked load that matters for rooftop tents. Driving loads are much lower, and the box and its contents count against the driving figure in your manual, not the 700 lb number. Wilderness owners also typically fit aftermarket bars (The Rack Shop lists 50 in bars) rather than using the standard trims' swing-out bars."),
 ("Will a roof box hit the Outback's rear gate?",
  "The Outback is a long wagon, so it has more room at the back of the roof than a compact SUV, but a long box can still reach the rear gate's path. Mount the box forward, then open the gate slowly the first time. If your Outback has a power rear gate with an adjustable opening height, you can lower that setting as a backup."),
 ("What size roof box is best for an Outback?",
  "A 16 cu ft box such as the Yakima SkyBox 16 or GrandTour 16 suits most families, and it leaves room under a roof limit of roughly 150–176 lb. Skiers should look at length rather than volume: the SkyBox NX Skinny takes skis up to 195 cm while leaving bar space. If you want the lightest box, the 30.2 lb DeepSpace 10 has a 100 lb cargo limit."),
 ("Do I need aftermarket crossbars for a roof box on an Outback?",
  "Not always. The swing-out bars work for occasional trips if their spread fits the box. Aftermarket bars make sense when you want a spread the factory bars can't reach (the DeepSpace 10 needs 32–46 in), a quieter aero bar, or a Wilderness setup. Buy bars listed for your Outback's rail type. Integrated-rail and Wilderness kits are different, and our Outback roof rack page lists both."),
 ("Can I carry skis and a cargo box on an Outback at the same time?",
  "Yes, with a narrow box. A full-width 16 cu ft box takes most of the crossbar length. The SkyBox NX Skinny is 26.5 in wide, and Yakima says it leaves crossbar space for other gear, so a ski or bike mount can go next to it. Add up the weight of the box, the second mount and the gear, and keep the total under the roof limit."),
 ("Do 2020–2025 Outback roof box setups carry over to the 2026 Outback?",
  "The box does; boxes clamp to crossbars, not to the car. The 2026 Outback is a new seventh generation, so the crossbars may not. Buy bars listed for the 2026 model and use its manual's roof figures. Reports on the 2026 Outback quote a 220 lb dynamic rating, which differs from the 6th-gen figures above."),
 ("Will a roof box block the Outback's sunroof?",
  "It shouldn't if you place the front crossbar thoughtfully. Keep the front bar and the front of the box clear of the glass panel's tilt and slide path, and open the sunroof once after mounting to confirm. The box's spread range usually leaves room to shift the bars a few inches."),
 ("Does a roof box hurt the Outback's fuel economy?",
  "Yes, any roof box adds drag, and the effect grows with speed. Yakima's boxes here have tapered noses, and a box mounted level and centered is quieter and more efficient than one that sits nose-up. The most effective step is taking the box off between trips; the SkyBox and GrandTour use quick-release mounts and Yakima quotes about 10 minutes to install."),
]

